  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 214 PM CST Sat Nov 21 2026\n\nThe extended forecast will feature much of the same weather expected \non Monday. Placement on the backside of persistent upper-level \ntroughing will keep CAA in place through the early part of the \nweek. While the resulting subsidence will promote dry weather, \nhighs on Tuesday are progged to only reach into the mid to \nupper 30s, with overnight lows ranging from the teens to the \nlower 20s. By Wednesday, a shortwave trough will begin to dig \nout of western Canada, inducing downstream upper-level ridging \nand height rises over the region. This synoptic shift will \nmaintain dry conditions while initiating a relative warming \ntrend, with daytime highs climbing back into the mid to upper \n40s beginning Wednesday and persisting through the remainder of \nthe week.",
